  "notes": "In ChatGPT GPT-5 is a system of a fast model, a reasoning model (GPT-5 thinking) and a router; in the API gpt-5 is the reasoning model, offered with mini and nano sizes, and the ChatGPT non-reasoning model was offered as gpt-5-chat-latest (src.openai.gpt-5-developers-announcement). GPT-5 mini, nano and pro are inline variants. The 2026-06-11 deprecation names gpt-5-2025-08-07, gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07, gpt-5-nano-2025-08-07 and gpt-5-pro-2025-10-06 with shutdown scheduled for 2026-12-11; retired is left empty until then. gpt-5-chat-latest was shut down on 2026-07-23 (deprecations page, 2026-04-22 entry, July 2026 shutdown). The announcement also lists GPT-4.5 among the ChatGPT models GPT-5 replaced; no relation is recorded for that because GPT-4.5's API replacement was GPT-4.1 and the system card does not map it. The system card maps GPT-4o mini to gpt-5-main-mini, a ChatGPT fallback model that is not an inline variant here, so no relation to openai.gpt-4o-mini is recorded."
